Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 08:28:36 -0800
Subject: Disallow differing origins in most synchronous about:blank commits

Problem: the synchronous about:blank commit origin check is loose in
ways that a compromised renderer can use to commit a document in a new
same-process frame with an origin it shouldn't have:
- When the browser-derived origin is opaque, it only compares the
  precursor, not the nonce. This lets the frame claim another
  cross-process document's opaque origin and get its StorageKey.
- When the browser-derived origin isn't opaque, it accepts any opaque
  origin from the renderer, including one with a file:// precursor. In
  an unlocked process (e.g. for most sites on Android), a later commit
  with that origin gets access to file: URLs.
- It skips the check entirely when the renderer reports a file: origin.

These exceptions were added for popups opened from CSP-sandboxed
documents with allow-popups-to-escape-sandbox, where the browser used
to derive a different origin than the renderer. crrev.com/c/7596676
fixed that, so the browser now derives the same origin as the renderer
for new frames: either inherited from the creator, or derived from a
sandbox origin token that the browser also sends to the renderer.

This CL requires the origins to match exactly, except in these cases,
which are temporary:
- When kUseSandboxTokenForOriginDerivation is disabled, opaque origins
  with the same precursor are still allowed. The feature will be
  removed in crrev.com/c/8692865.
- Opaque origins without a precursor are still allowed to differ. The
  renderer creates these on its own for main frames without a creator
  or reused after a crash, so the browser can't predict them yet. They
  aren't tied to any site, so they can't be used to get another site's
  origin or access to file: URLs. crrev.com/c/8690429 will make the
  browser pick these origins.
- File origins only skip the check if the browser also expects a file
  origin, until https://crbug.com/582733579 is fixed.

